young things on the beach

1311
01:07:18,635 --> 01:07:22,139
just happened to be
you 20 years ago.

1312
01:07:22,139 --> 01:07:24,641
Just thinking of
your protection.

1313
01:07:24,641 --> 01:07:25,309
Chin chin.

1314
01:07:47,797 --> 01:07:50,300
Hello, Detective.

1315
01:07:50,300 --> 01:07:51,868
How long will he be gone?

1316
01:07:51,868 --> 01:07:54,003
Two days.

1317
01:07:54,003 --> 01:07:57,841
Nora, let's
just get out of here.

1318
01:07:57,841 --> 01:07:59,343
And do what?

1319
01:07:59,343 --> 01:08:00,744
I'm about
a step and a half

1320
01:08:00,744 --> 01:08:03,780
away from finding that
recording, and I will get it.

1321
01:08:03,780 --> 01:08:05,349
And if Jack Wolfe
shows up dead, I

1322
01:08:05,349 --> 01:08:07,584
will have no choice
but to arrest you.

1323
01:08:07,584 --> 01:08:08,485
Will you?

1324
01:08:08,485 --> 01:08:09,453
Believe it.

1325
01:08:09,453 --> 01:08:10,987
Just call her off, Nora.

1326
01:08:10,987 --> 01:08:12,289
Why?

1327
01:08:12,289 --> 01:08:14,491
Because the last thing on
Earth I want is to arrest you.

1328
01:08:14,491 --> 01:08:15,959
Really?

1329
01:08:15,959 --> 01:08:18,195
And what do you
want to do with me?

1330
01:08:18,195 --> 01:08:21,798
You want to take me away, and
we live happily ever after?

1331
01:08:21,798 --> 01:08:23,700
Yeah.

1332
01:08:23,700 --> 01:08:25,034
Dani, you're such a fool.

1333
01:08:25,034 --> 01:08:25,869
We could have everything.

1334
01:08:25,869 --> 01:08:26,970
All I want is you.

1335
01:08:26,970 --> 01:08:32,909
Then I tell you what.

1336
01:08:32,909 --> 01:08:36,413
When Jack turns up dead, you
forget about the recording

1337
01:08:36,413 --> 01:08:38,047
and arrest Chad.

1338
01:08:38,047 --> 01:08:42,786
Then you can have
me and the money.

1339
01:08:42,786 --> 01:08:45,722
Jealous man can
always be used for something.

1340
01:08:45,722 --> 01:08:46,423
Is that right?

1341
01:08:46,423 --> 01:08:47,557
Ugh.

1342
01:08:47,557 --> 01:08:48,758
You're the one I wanted.

1343
01:08:48,758 --> 01:08:51,461
You're the one
I've always wanted.

1344
01:08:51,461 --> 01:08:55,131
If you want to stop it, shoot
me, arrest me, shoot Jack.

1345
01:08:55,131 --> 01:08:57,100
But just do something.

1346
01:08:57,100 --> 01:08:59,503
Because if you
don't, I'm trapped.

1347
01:08:59,503 --> 01:09:01,971
I don't have a choice.

1348
01:09:19,389 --> 01:09:21,958
All right, good.

1349
01:09:21,958 --> 01:09:23,693
You're sulking.

1350
01:09:23,693 --> 01:09:25,429
Sulking makes you
look suspicious.

1351
01:09:25,429 --> 01:09:27,030
Come on, perk up.

1352
01:09:27,030 --> 01:09:29,333
Give me that, the
girls love me, face.

1353
01:09:29,333 --> 01:09:31,167
Come on.

1354
01:09:31,167 --> 01:09:34,170
Yes.

1355
01:09:34,170 --> 01:09:36,206
Perfecto!

1356
01:09:36,206 --> 01:09:37,407
You handsome devil.

1357
01:09:40,109 --> 01:09:42,246
Why are you sulking?

1358
01:09:42,246 --> 01:09:44,113
Oh, man, I think
she was with that guy

1359
01:09:44,113 --> 01:09:46,216
again the other day
when you were in Miami.

1360
01:09:46,216 --> 01:09:48,618
You know, the gardener saw
them go into your place.

1361
01:09:48,618 --> 01:09:49,486
What guy?

1362
01:09:49,486 --> 01:09:51,388
Well, the
cop who hit me, man.

1363
01:09:51,388 --> 01:09:52,055
No!

1364
01:09:52,055 --> 01:09:52,889
Yeah!

1365
01:09:52,889 --> 01:09:54,157
Shocking!

1366
01:09:54,157 --> 01:09:55,792
Well, what do you think?

1367
01:09:55,792 --> 01:09:56,326
Well--

1368
01:09:56,326 --> 01:09:57,193
Uh-uh.

1369
01:09:57,193 --> 01:09:59,028
Are you jealous
that she's playing

1370
01:09:59,028 --> 01:10:01,765
hanky panky behind your back?

1371
01:10:01,765 --> 01:10:02,499
No, dude.

1372
01:10:02,499 --> 01:10:03,132
No.

1373
01:10:03,132 --> 01:10:04,701
See, it's with the cop.

1374
01:10:04,701 --> 01:10:08,405
I mean, what if she says, you
know, if Jack winds up dead,

1375
01:10:08,405 --> 01:10:11,140
you bust Chad, and then
she and him go and boogie

1376
01:10:11,140 --> 01:10:13,277
down to the Bahamas, man?

1377
01:10:13,277 --> 01:10:16,112
That's outstanding, Chad!

1378
01:10:16,112 --> 01:10:18,915
Excellent, my boy!

1379
01:10:18,915 --> 01:10:21,885
You see, you've only been my
adopted son for a short time,

1380
01:10:21,885 --> 01:10:23,953
and already your IQ is up.

1381
01:10:23,953 --> 01:10:25,221
Thank you, man.

1382
01:10:25,221 --> 01:10:29,158
But allow me to posit
another idea that could perhaps

1383
01:10:29,158 --> 01:10:34,197
be even more problematic.

1384
01:10:34,197 --> 01:10:37,634
What's more problematic
than getting arrested, dude?

1385
01:10:37,634 --> 01:10:41,505
Oh, what if Nora
decides to dump you,

1386
01:10:41,505 --> 01:10:45,342
and then she remembers that
Chad is the only person who

1387
01:10:45,342 --> 01:10:47,076
knows I'm guilty of murder?

1388
01:10:47,076 --> 01:10:49,546
Therefore, she says
to herself, Chad's

1389
01:10:49,546 --> 01:10:51,515
the only person who
can put me in prison

1390
01:10:51,515 --> 01:10:53,116
for the rest of my life.

1391
01:10:53,116 --> 01:11:01,391
Then she says, I've got to--

1392
01:11:01,391 --> 01:11:03,693
I gotta kill Chad.

1393
01:11:03,693 --> 01:11:08,264
Positively, Jean, my son.

1394
01:11:12,369 --> 01:11:18,575
Lovey, I don't know if our Chad
has confided this to you or not,

1395
01:11:18,575 --> 01:11:22,546
but I suggested to
him the other day

1396
01:11:22,546 --> 01:11:25,915
that after he and I fake
my death, that both of us

1397
01:11:25,915 --> 01:11:28,318
should kill you.

1398
01:11:28,318 --> 01:11:30,053
Then Jean gets the money.

1399
01:11:30,053 --> 01:11:34,558
And naturally, he shares
it with dear old papa.

1400
01:11:34,558 --> 01:11:37,193
I think he's taken quite
a shine to the idea.

1401
01:11:37,193 --> 01:11:40,997
You know, he doesn't trust
you anymore, querida.

1402
01:11:40,997 --> 01:11:44,868
Quite frankly,
he's afraid of you.

1403
01:11:44,868 --> 01:11:45,469
Is he?

1404
01:11:45,469 --> 01:11:47,036
Mm-hmm.

1405
01:11:47,036 --> 01:11:50,574
But you know I never hide
anything from you, mi amor.

1406
01:11:55,579 --> 01:11:58,948
I know you think I'm
a liar, duplicitous.

1407
01:11:58,948 --> 01:12:04,954
But I think I am the most
constant of life's companions.

1408
01:12:04,954 --> 01:12:08,825
I say we stick to
the original plan.

1409
01:12:08,825 --> 01:12:11,294
Pin my murder on
Chad, split the money,

1410
01:12:11,294 --> 01:12:16,332
and I give you the
ultimate gift of love.

1411
01:12:16,332 --> 01:12:18,702
I set you free.

1412
01:12:18,702 --> 01:12:22,672
I swear to God, Nora.

1413
01:12:22,672 --> 01:12:25,308
I love you.

1414
01:12:25,308 --> 01:12:27,176
I do.

1415
01:12:27,176 --> 01:12:32,516
I know you think I'm
lying, but I do love you.

1416
01:12:32,516 --> 01:12:35,452
Siempre, amore mio.

1417
01:12:35,452 --> 01:12:39,723
I love you because you and
I are exactly the same.

1418
01:12:39,723 --> 01:12:44,027
The world judges us harshly,
but I don't judge you at all.

1419
01:12:44,027 --> 01:12:49,198
Even when I know you and lover
boy are planning to kill me,

1420
01:12:49,198 --> 01:12:51,334
I know and I don't judge you.

1421
01:12:53,837 --> 01:12:56,172
God, I hate this.

1422
01:12:56,840 --> 01:12:58,374
Oh, no, no, no, no.

1423
01:12:58,374 --> 01:12:59,876
Shh.

1424
01:12:59,876 --> 01:13:00,944
Hush, little kitten.

1425
01:13:00,944 --> 01:13:02,412
No.

1426
01:13:02,412 --> 01:13:05,549
It's all right.

1427
01:13:05,549 --> 01:13:08,652
So tell me.

1428
01:13:08,652 --> 01:13:14,591
Even when I know you're going
to kill me, what should I do?

1429
01:13:14,591 --> 01:13:15,492
Hmm?

1430
01:13:17,694 --> 01:13:22,666
In my place, Nora,
what would you do?

1431
01:13:22,666 --> 01:13:24,167
Kill me.

1432
01:13:24,167 --> 01:13:26,302
Hmm.

1433
01:13:26,302 --> 01:13:28,505
See?

1434
01:13:28,505 --> 01:13:30,306
I never lie to you.

1435
01:13:30,306 --> 01:13:33,342
No, you never lie.

1436
01:13:33,342 --> 01:13:36,345
All right.

1437
01:13:36,345 --> 01:13:39,248
So let's plan my death.

1438
01:13:41,885 --> 01:13:44,120
Put this in the engine
room, and hurry.

1439
01:13:44,120 --> 01:13:45,822
You've got 15 minutes.

1440
01:13:45,822 --> 01:13:49,092
Jean, I'm proud of you, son.

1441
01:14:22,859 --> 01:14:24,761
Jack?

1442
01:14:24,761 --> 01:14:25,261
Jack?

1443
01:14:32,135 --> 01:14:36,239
Promise me that
you'll consider this, Nora.

1444
01:14:36,239 --> 01:14:42,546
'Cause if not, then I'll have no
choice but to help him kill you.

1445
01:14:46,616 --> 01:14:49,919
No more games.

1446
01:14:49,919 --> 01:14:51,621
No more games.

1447
01:14:52,722 --> 01:14:56,359
This works on the
parasympathetic nervous system.

1448
01:14:56,359 --> 01:14:58,962
It's called pilocarpine.

1449
01:14:58,962 --> 01:15:00,964
I've had some
experience with it.

1450
01:15:00,964 --> 01:15:03,099
But she won't feel a thing.

1451
01:15:03,099 --> 01:15:05,501
Her throat will constrict.

1452
01:15:05,501 --> 01:15:06,736
She'll choke a bit.

1453
01:15:06,736 --> 01:15:09,005
And there'll be some
gasping for air.

1454
01:15:09,005 --> 01:15:11,808
It's called paraldehyde.

1455
01:15:11,808 --> 01:15:16,279
Toxicity level 5,
reaction time immediate.

1456
01:15:16,279 --> 01:15:20,183
His heart spasms, head feels
like it's about to explode.

1457
01:15:21,651 --> 01:15:23,953
There will be bronchial
constriction, wheezing.

1458
01:15:23,953 --> 01:15:25,121
The muscles will twitch.

1459
01:15:25,121 --> 01:15:26,255
The pulse will slow.

1460
01:15:26,255 --> 01:15:28,124
And convulsions will ensue.

1461
01:15:28,124 --> 01:15:32,796
You hit him with it in
the shoulder or in the back,

1462
01:15:32,796 --> 01:15:34,363
wherever.

1463
01:15:38,968 --> 01:15:44,674
Et voila, death by
asphyxia and cardiac arrest.

1464
01:15:44,674 --> 01:15:48,211
One shot, et voila.

1465
01:15:48,211 --> 01:15:49,779
It's over.

1466
01:15:49,779 --> 01:15:53,717
Well, you see, Lovey,
I attach the yellow wire here,

1467
01:15:53,717 --> 01:15:59,488
like so, and the
blue one into here.

1468
01:15:59,488 --> 01:16:03,259
In this scenario, I tell Chad--

1469
01:16:03,259 --> 01:16:04,628
Bomb in the engine room.

1470
01:16:04,628 --> 01:16:05,662
I'll be waiting for you.

1471
01:16:05,662 --> 01:16:06,462
All right?

1472
01:16:06,462 --> 01:16:07,130
Come on.

1473
01:16:07,130 --> 01:16:07,864
Get it done.

1474
01:16:07,864 --> 01:16:08,998
We can get the hell out of here.

1475
01:16:08,998 --> 01:16:10,299
Awesome, man.

1476
01:16:15,304 --> 01:16:16,339
You're done?

1477
01:16:16,339 --> 01:16:17,340
All set, man.

1478
01:16:21,878 --> 01:16:24,681
He trusts me implicitly.

1479
01:16:24,681 --> 01:16:30,887
Such a lovely boy,
but thick as a brick.

1480
01:16:36,359 --> 01:16:38,662
Yes, got it.

1481
01:16:38,662 --> 01:16:39,829
His name's Perez.

1482
01:16:39,829 --> 01:16:40,429
Who?

1483
01:16:40,429 --> 01:16:44,267
Jack's flunky.

1484
01:16:44,267 --> 01:16:46,569
He's too cheap to pay anybody
anything without getting

1485
01:16:46,569 --> 01:16:49,538
a tax write off for it.

1486
01:16:49,538 --> 01:16:52,208
See here?

1487
01:16:52,208 --> 01:16:54,243
He listed someone
named Anibal Perez

1488
01:16:54,243 --> 01:16:57,180
as a gardener for his business.

1489
01:16:57,180 --> 01:16:59,282
Here's the same
Anibal Perez listed

1490
01:16:59,282 --> 01:17:01,885
as a handyman two years later.

1491
01:17:01,885 --> 01:17:06,790
And here is the same
Perez listed as a janitor.

1492
01:17:06,790 --> 01:17:09,592
Now all we need is an address.

1493
01:17:09,592 --> 01:17:13,697
Then we get the voice
recorder and kill Jack.

1494
01:17:13,697 --> 01:17:15,799
The
guy's name is Perez.

1495
01:17:15,799 --> 01:17:17,166
Anibal Perez.

1496
01:17:17,166 --> 01:17:18,835
You got an
address for us?

1497
01:17:18,835 --> 01:17:20,136
No, no.

1498
01:17:20,136 --> 01:17:21,738
I don't know no address.

1499
01:17:41,257 --> 01:17:43,359
Jack tampered with it.

1500
01:17:43,359 --> 01:17:46,329
He'll tell you to set
the timer for 15 minutes

1501
01:17:46,329 --> 01:17:48,097
while he waits in the dinghy.

1502
01:17:48,097 --> 01:17:51,200
But it'll explode
after 3 minutes.

1503
01:17:51,200 --> 01:17:55,739
So once you get him on the boat,
hit him with the paraldehyde.

1504
01:18:00,744 --> 01:18:06,082
And then use this.

1505
01:18:06,082 --> 01:18:09,585
Put both bombs on the boat,
but only trigger this one.

1506
01:18:09,585 --> 01:18:12,621
Set it for 10 minutes, which
will leave you plenty of time

1507
01:18:12,621 --> 01:18:13,723
to get out of there.

1508
01:18:18,828 --> 01:18:20,964
The biggest mistake
my husband ever made

1509
01:18:20,964 --> 01:18:26,002
was showing me how
to build a bomb.

1510
01:19:22,992 --> 01:19:26,162
That'll be Jack, Mr. Perez.

1511
01:19:26,162 --> 01:19:29,498
Now, give me the voice recorder
and the videos, or you're dead.

1512
01:19:29,498 --> 01:19:32,001
What recorder?

1513
01:19:32,001 --> 01:19:33,002
Mira.

1514
01:19:33,002 --> 01:19:34,737
I don't know nothing.

1515
01:19:34,737 --> 01:19:36,305
I'll count to three.

1516
01:19:36,305 --> 01:19:39,075
And either what I want
is on its way to my hand,

1517
01:19:39,075 --> 01:19:42,611
or your brains are on
their way to that wall.

1518
01:19:42,611 --> 01:19:44,247
Please, Señora.

1519
01:19:44,247 --> 01:19:44,780
What recorder?

1520
01:19:44,780 --> 01:19:46,349
1, 2--

1521
01:19:46,349 --> 01:19:47,416
Drop it, Nora.

1522
01:19:50,987 --> 01:19:51,955
It's over.

1523
01:19:54,423 --> 01:19:56,993
You'd kill me, Dani?

1524
01:19:56,993 --> 01:19:57,827
Is that true?

1525
01:19:57,827 --> 01:20:00,163
You'd kill me?

1526
01:20:03,132 --> 01:20:05,869
He wouldn't have to.

1527
01:20:05,869 --> 01:20:06,836
I would.

1528
01:20:11,740 --> 01:20:14,377
Dr. Castro,
the remains of Chad Sellers

1529
01:20:14,377 --> 01:20:17,380
were found and shipped by our
department to your laboratory

1530
01:20:17,380 --> 01:20:18,848
for DNA testing.

1531
01:20:18,848 --> 01:20:21,717
They included the fibia and
tibia bone, respectively.

1532
01:20:21,717 --> 01:20:23,920
They were then matched
against hair samples found

1533
01:20:23,920 --> 01:20:26,055
in Mr. Sellers' apartment.

1534
01:20:26,055 --> 01:20:29,225
And your conclusion
was what, Dr. Castro?

1535
01:20:29,225 --> 01:20:30,994
The DNA
match between the bones

1536
01:20:30,994 --> 01:20:33,863
pulled out of the water and
the hair sample was positive.

1537
01:20:33,863 --> 01:20:35,798
I have not the slightest
doubt that those were

1538
01:20:35,798 --> 01:20:37,266
the remains of Mr. Sellers.

1539
01:20:37,266 --> 01:20:39,502
Likewise,
there was a blood splatter

1540
01:20:39,502 --> 01:20:42,338
on a piece of decking which
was ultimately recovered,

1541
01:20:42,338 --> 01:20:44,140
and one tooth, which
was also shipped

1542
01:20:44,140 --> 01:20:46,009
to your department for testing.

1543
01:20:46,009 --> 01:20:47,843
What were the results
of those tests?

1544
01:20:47,843 --> 01:20:50,246
The blood splatters
and the tooth in question,

1545
01:20:50,246 --> 01:20:52,848
which, by the way, feature
a very distinctive cap that

1546
01:20:52,848 --> 01:20:57,586
would only have been available
in Cuba between 1945 and 1958,

1547
01:20:57,586 --> 01:21:00,623
were positively matched with
known DNA samples of Mr. Jack

1548
01:21:00,623 --> 01:21:01,624
Wolfe.

1549
01:21:11,167 --> 01:21:13,736
Lieutenant
Fuentes, the head

1550
01:21:13,736 --> 01:21:16,339
of the bomb squad for the
San Miguel State Police

1551
01:21:16,339 --> 01:21:17,840
for the area of Puerto Seguro.

1552
01:21:17,840 --> 01:21:19,208
Is that all correct?

1553
01:21:19,208 --> 01:21:20,443
Yes, sir.

1554
01:21:20,443 --> 01:21:21,844
Were you able
to determine the cause

1555
01:21:21,844 --> 01:21:24,747
of the explosion which occurred
on the motor yacht Circe

1556
01:21:24,747 --> 01:21:26,549
on the morning of the 15th?

1557
01:21:26,549 --> 01:21:29,152
Well, there
were two explosions, actually,

1558
01:21:29,152 --> 01:21:30,987
two separate bombs.

1559
01:21:30,987 --> 01:21:32,588
The triggering
device, however, seems

1560
01:21:32,588 --> 01:21:35,791
to have come from a bomb
planted in the engine room.

1561
01:21:35,791 --> 01:21:38,661
The marina surveillance caught
the whole thing on tape,

1562
01:21:38,661 --> 01:21:41,664
and we were able to recover
part of the bomb's timing device

1563
01:21:41,664 --> 01:21:43,432
from the ocean floor.

1564
01:21:51,740 --> 01:21:53,776
Detective, I'm going

1565
01:21:53,776 --> 01:21:57,213
to show you a voice recorder.

1566
01:21:57,213 --> 01:21:59,748
Prosecution's exhibit 52.

1567
